    "voice.consent.cloud": {
      "comment": "One-time consent before the first cloud Creole use. 'We don't keep it' is a server requirement (Creole report 7.2) that must be true of the deployed proxy before shipping. | es: Miami Spanish (US Spanish, usted where addressed), agent-authored; no human review record yet. UNCERTAIN: the no-retention promise must match the deployed server; wording fine, content pending. | ht: Haitian Creole drafted by the myAD Language agent from general knowledge of standard Kreyòl orthography (Akademi Kreyòl Ayisyen spelling). Not reviewed by a native speaker; must stay needs_review until a human native-speaker pass (decision D9). Based on the Creole report's unreviewed draft ('Pou m tande Kreyòl, vwa ou ap pase sou yon sèvè; nou pa kenbe l'). | ht casing: 'kreyòl' vs 'Kreyòl' (and 'kre yòl' variants) is inconsistent across strings; the native reviewer should pick one. Not changed by the agent.",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "To understand Kreyòl, your voice goes through our server. We don't keep it. Is that OK?"
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "Para entender Kreyòl, su voz pasa por nuestro servidor. No la guardamos. ¿Está de acuerdo?"
          }
        },
        "ht": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "Pou nou tande kreyòl, vwa ou ap pase sou sèvè nou an. Nou pa kenbe l. Ou dakò?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "voice.consent.never": {
      "comment": "Permanent switch: neither the voice (listening) nor card text (server read-aloud) leaves the phone; Kreyòl falls back to tapping and on-screen text. | es: Miami Spanish (US Spanish, usted where addressed), agent-authored; no human review record yet. | ht: Haitian Creole drafted by the myAD Language agent from general knowledge of standard Kreyòl orthography (Akademi Kreyòl Ayisyen spelling). Not reviewed by a native speaker; must stay needs_review until a human native-speaker pass (decision D9).",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Never send my voice or card text to our server"
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "No enviar nunca mi voz ni el texto de las tarjetas a nuestro servidor"
          }
        },
        "ht": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "Pa janm voye vwa mwen ni tèks kat yo bay sèvè nou an"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "voice.consent.readAloud": {
      "comment": "One-time consent before the first server read-aloud of a Kreyòl card (speech OUT; separate from voice.consent.cloud, which is about the person's voice). Asked only when a server Kreyòl voice exists. Do NOT add a retention sentence ('We don't keep the words') until the deployed server's retention is confirmed. | es: Miami Spanish (US Spanish, usted where addressed), agent-authored; no human review record yet. | ht: Haitian Creole drafted by the myAD Language agent from general knowledge of standard Kreyòl orthography (Akademi Kreyòl Ayisyen spelling). Not reviewed by a native speaker; must stay needs_review until a human native-speaker pass (decision D9). | ht casing: 'kreyòl' vs 'Kreyòl' (and 'kre yòl' variants) is inconsistent across strings; the native reviewer should pick one. Not changed by the agent.",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "To read this aloud in Kreyòl, the app sends the card's words to our server. Your voice is not sent. Is that OK?"
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Para leer esto en voz alta en Kreyòl, la app envía las palabras de la tarjeta a nuestro servidor. Su voz no se envía. ¿Está de acuerdo?"
          }
        },
        "ht": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "Pou li sa a awotvwa an Kreyòl, aplikasyon an voye mo kat la bay sèvè nou an. Li pa voye vwa ou. Ou dakò?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "voice.creole.commandsOnly": {
      "comment": "ht surface, no Kreyòl listening, but on-device Spanish/English commands work. %1$@ = \"en español\" (Spanish-tagged), %2$@ = \"in English\" (English-tagged), %3$@ = the back phrase (\"atrás\" Spanish-tagged on es/ht; \"back\" on en). Filled by VoiceKey.creoleCommandsOnlyNotice from the bundled command lexicon; keep the quotes around each placeholder. | es: Miami Spanish (US Spanish, usted where addressed), agent-authored; no human review record yet. | ht: Haitian Creole drafted by the myAD Language agent from general knowledge of standard Kreyòl orthography (Akademi Kreyòl Ayisyen spelling). Not reviewed by a native speaker; must stay needs_review until a human native-speaker pass (decision D9). | ht casing: 'kreyòl' vs 'Kreyòl' (and 'kre yòl' variants) is inconsistent across strings; the native reviewer should pick one. Not changed by the agent.",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "I can't understand Kreyòl here yet. You can say \"%1$@\", \"%2$@\" or \"%3$@\", or use the buttons."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Todavía no entiendo Kreyòl aquí. Puede decir \"%1$@\", \"%2$@\" o \"%3$@\", o usar los botones."
          }
        },
        "ht": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "Mwen poko ka konprann Kreyòl isit la. Ou ka di \"%1$@\", \"%2$@\" oswa \"%3$@\", oswa sèvi ak bouton yo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "voice.creole.voiceOverLimit": {
      "comment": "Part of the Creole notice (A11Y-LANG-03 part 2): shown and announced with voice.unavailable.creole and kreyol.noRecording. States that the person's own VoiceOver may use another language's voice for Kreyòl, while the app's own read-aloud never does. | es: Miami Spanish (US Spanish, usted where addressed), agent-authored; no human review record yet. | ht: Haitian Creole drafted by the myAD Language agent from general knowledge of standard Kreyòl orthography (Akademi Kreyòl Ayisyen spelling). Not reviewed by a native speaker; must stay needs_review until a human native-speaker pass (decision D9). | ht casing: 'kreyòl' vs 'Kreyòl' (and 'kre yòl' variants) is inconsistent across strings; the native reviewer should pick one. Not changed by the agent.",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "VoiceOver may read Kreyòl with another language's voice. This app's voice never does that."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "VoiceOver puede leer el Kreyòl con la voz de otro idioma. La voz de esta app nunca lo hace."
          }
        },
        "ht": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "VoiceOver ka li Kreyòl ak vwa yon lòt lang. Vwa aplikasyon sa a pa janm fè sa."
          }
        }
      }
    },
